msgid "Authorize access to web endpoints"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To control which callers can access the web endpoints of a {project-name} "
"application, define authorization rules with security annotations or HTTP "
"security policies for request paths.\n"
"When security is active, {project-name} checks every HTTP request against "
"these rules to determine whether it can proceed."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Most authorization rules check the roles and permissions of the "
"`SecurityIdentity` that represents the caller.\n"
"The security identity provider supplies the roles.\n"
"To customize them, create a `SecurityIdentityAugmentor`, as described in "
"xref:security-customization.adoc#security-identity-customization[Security "
"Identity Customization]."
msgstr ""

msgid "Authorize requests in configuration"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To protect paths without a change to the code, define HTTP permissions in "
"the `application.properties` file.\n"
"Each permission set names paths, optionally HTTP methods, and the policy "
"that decides whether a request to those paths can proceed."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Be careful when you create complex, possibly overlapping HTTP security "
"policy path expressions.\n"
"Make sure that there are no typos in the configured policy paths.\n"
"Be aware that the root path is only prepended to the policy paths that do "
"not start with a forward slash, for more information, see the <<permission-"
"paths-and-root-paths>> section.\n"
"Test your HTTP policy configuration thoroughly, verify that the allowed "
"requests succeed and that the requests with invalid credentials or\n"
"insufficient permissions are rejected.\n"
"If you work with Jakarta RESTful Web Services (Jakarta REST) endpoints, "
"prefer <<standard-security-annotations,standard security annotations>> to "
"the path-based HTTP security policies."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If you work with Jakarta REST endpoints and need to set default security "
"requirements, prefer using <<standard-security-annotations,standard security "
"annotations>> and the `quarkus.security.jaxrs.deny-unannotated-endpoints` or "
"`quarkus.security.jaxrs.default-roles-allowed` property instead of HTTP "
"security policy path matching, see <<configuration-properties-to-deny-"
"access>>.\n"
"Security annotations can override these properties on an individual Jakarta "
"REST resource or method."
msgstr ""

